      "content": "What you're describing sounds like a profound sense of loss, as if a fundamental part of your identity has disappeared. When the foundation of who you were is gone, the daily routine can feel utterly meaningless and forced. It's okay to feel like you're just going through the motions right now; that's a natural response to such a massive shift. Please know that even in this quiet, shell-like state, there is still a core of *you* underneath all of it.",
      "source": "target",
