      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's incredibly brave of you to articulate how completely tied your sense of self was to that connection. When the external scaffolding of your life is removed, it leaves a vast, terrifying emptiness. If the \"self\" you built was dependent on another, then it makes perfect sense that it feels hollow now. Consider that letting the lights go out isn't the only option; just allowing yourself to *be* in the emptiness without the pressure to fix it might be a small, necessary step.",
